title start
kind: note
tags: business-plan conventions link-conventions-between-pages
Conventions link conventions between pages
title end

paragraph start
The notation has no link syntax yet, so a page refers to another page by writing its exact file name in a paragraph, including the number and the area key.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Because numbers can change, every reference is found by searching for the old name when a folder is renumbered. A reference never uses a short or informal name.
paragraph end

paragraph start
An area key is never reused by another area, so a file name stays unique in the whole tree even when numbers repeat.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: add link support to the notation, or a tool that rewrites references on renumbering
Until then references are updated by hand.
paragraph end

